      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Giant coronary aneurysms are rare and often confused with cardiac tumours."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "OBSERVATION",
          "content": "We report a new case of this type of aneurysm occurring on the right coronary artery revealed by a cardiac congestion."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "COMMENTS",
          "content": "These aneurysms can be due to inflammatory diseases or dysplasia. But in these pseudotumoral forms, atherosclerosis is the main aetiology. The diagnosis and treatment require surgery and histological examination."
        }
      ]},
